-- allium: 3
-- librarian-runtime.allium

-- Scope: ejecución embebida y gobernada de la bibliotecaria de una Vera.
-- Includes: constitución, configuración de inferencia por referencia, ciclo de
--   vida, solicitudes, ronda diaria, recibos y coexistencia con un puente externo.
-- Excludes: custodia material del secreto y semántica de cada modelo.

use "./core.allium" as core
use "./agent-manifest.allium" as manifests
use "./agent-conversation.allium" as conversations
use "./owner-librarian-harness.allium" as harnesses

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

contract ResidentLibrarianExecution {
    answer_request: (configuration: LibrarianRuntimeConfiguration, request: conversations/ConversationRequest) -> conversations/AgentReply

    @invariant ConversationContinuityIsEffectiveContext
        -- Every inference receives a bounded chronological projection of the
        -- conversation, including the original unresolved instruction, human
        -- contributions, prior replies and the current turn. A new turn never
        -- reduces the task to its last sentence.

    @invariant GovernanceAndOntologyAreResidentContext
        -- The effective property vocabulary, semantic objects, relation
        -- definitions, special pages and corpus-writing grammar travel with the
        -- task or are available through built-in tools. They are part of the
        -- resident office, not optional MCP lore.

    @invariant SourcePageAndFocusAreAlwaysMicroContext
        -- Every request made from a page carries that page's identity,
        -- properties and revision plus a bounded, ordered projection of its
        -- blocks. A block request also carries the exact focus, ancestors,
        -- siblings and descendants needed to read it in place. The snapshot
        -- records its selection reason, budget and omissions instead of
        -- presenting a truncation as the whole page.

    @invariant RelevantLibraryNeighbourhoodIsMacroContext
        -- Before inference, Vera deterministically composes a bounded macro
        -- context from visible graph neighbours and text-search candidates.
        -- Every included page records why it was selected, a score equal to its
        -- visible signal contributions, and whether those contributions came
        -- from authorised graph distance or transparent text relevance. The
        -- model may read more through tools, but it never has to guess that a
        -- library exists.

    @invariant ContextSelectionLeavesAnAuditableReceipt
        -- The frozen context names every selected page and block, how it was
        -- found, why it was included, its current revision and authorship, the
        -- graph relations actually supplied, the exact character budget, every
        -- omission, warnings and a continuation whenever selection was partial.

    @invariant ContextNeverCrossesItsAuthorizedUniverse
        -- Authorization precedes ranking and traversal. Every page, block and
        -- relation named by the receipt belongs to its explicit within set;
        -- an inaccessible hit behaves as if it did not exist.

    @invariant ExposureAndContextReceiptMeasureTheSameDelivery
        -- Immediately before inference, the compact exposure log records the
        -- receipt's exact serialized volume and number of distinct delivered
        -- identities. It does not copy their text or structure into another
        -- persistent index.

    @invariant ToolProtocolNeverBecomesLibraryContent
        -- A valid or malformed tool request is protocol, never a final reply and
        -- never a block. Markdown fences around structured calls do not turn
        -- them into prose; rejected calls remain recoverable runtime failures.

    @invariant NegativeFindingsRequireRecordedEvidence
        -- The librarian cannot claim that pages, projects, tasks or relations do
        -- not exist without at least one successful relevant corpus inspection.
        -- Contradictory positive hits force another answer instead of inscription.

    @invariant DraftsAreValidatedBeforeTheyBecomeProposals
        -- Page properties and block edits are checked against current identity,
        -- revisions, ontology, target subject and value grammar before they can
        -- accompany a reply as reviewable changes.

    @invariant DailyWritingUsesTheLibrariansOwnSection
        -- When a request explicitly targets today's journal, the visible reply
        -- is a child of the single daily root "Bitácora de <agent name>". Vera
        -- creates the private journal and its bitácora type on first use when
        -- necessary, preserving ordinary agent_generation authorship.

    @invariant ConversationSummaryAndCorpusWorkAreDifferentObjects
        -- The conversational reply is a short account of what the librarian
        -- understood and did. Substantive work is a structured inscription in
        -- Vera and may target any governed page; it is never flattened into the
        -- chat message or into one oversized Markdown block.

    @invariant CorpusWritingIsARealBlockTree
        -- Each semantic unit is one block. Parent and position express the
        -- hierarchy; indentation, Markdown headings and list markers inside a
        -- string never impersonate child blocks. The server validates the whole
        -- tree before applying it atomically with agent_generation authorship.

    @invariant TheDailyRootIsReservedStructure
        -- The one root "Bitácora de <agent name>" is stable infrastructure. A
        -- librarian may add, edit, move or remove descendants but cannot alter,
        -- move or remove that root through an ordinary request.

    @invariant EveryRemovalIsDeclaredTwice
        -- A destructive corpus operation is accepted only when the short chat
        -- reply names what was removed and why, and the same declaration is
        -- written automatically under today's own librarian journal. A removal
        -- can therefore never succeed silently, even when its target is elsewhere.

    @invariant ResidentAuthorityDoesNotEraseHistory
        -- The resident librarian may curate throughout the governed Vera with
        -- the owner's configured authority. Edits, moves and removals still use
        -- fresh revisions, ordinary operations, lineage and recoverable history;
        -- broad reach is not an exemption from provenance.

    @invariant IdentitySurvivesRuntimeAndProviderChanges
        -- Lucienne's participant, office, conversations, harness, authorship and
        -- history do not belong to Qwen, Codex, OpenClaw or any other runtime or
        -- model provider. The owner may replace either execution adapter or
        -- provider without replacing the librarian.

    @invariant TheConfiguredRuntimeIsTheOnlyRuntime
        -- A request is dispatched only through the execution adapter and model
        -- chosen by the owner. Failure leaves the durable request recoverable;
        -- Vera never falls back silently from Codex to a local model, from one
        -- provider to another, or from an external agent to embedded inference.
}

enum LibrarianRunKind { request | routine }
enum LibrarianRunState { running | completed | failed }
enum LibrarianExecutionAdapter { embedded_model | external_agent }
enum LibrarianRuntimePermission { read_request_context | reply | daily_round }
enum FormativePractice { reading | selection | interpretation | comparison | synthesis | conclusion }
enum DialecticGateStatus { open | responding | fulfilled | bypassed }
enum ContextDiscovery { focus | structure | page_start | text_match | graph_neighbour }

entity LibrarianCorpusInscription {
    request: conversations/ConversationRequest
    reply: conversations/AgentReply
    librarian: core/Participant
    blocks: List<LibrarianInscribedBlock>
    changes: List<core/Change>
    removals: List<LibrarianRemovalDeclaration>
    created_at: Timestamp
}

entity LibrarianInscribedBlock {
    inscription: LibrarianCorpusInscription
    key: String
    page: core/Page
    parent_key: String?
    position: Integer
    content: String
    materialized_block: core/Block
}

entity LibrarianRemovalDeclaration {
    inscription: LibrarianCorpusInscription
    subject: String
    reason: String
    chat_declaration: String
    journal_block: core/Block
}

entity LibrarianRuntimeConfiguration {
    librarian: harnesses/OwnerLibrarian
    enabled: Boolean
    adapter: LibrarianExecutionAdapter
    external_agent_id: String?
    model_id: String?
    endpoint: String?
    secret_reference: String?
    permissions: List<LibrarianRuntimePermission>
    dialectic_enabled: Boolean
    routine_enabled: Boolean
    routine_hour: Integer
    routine_timezone: String
    context_budget_characters: Integer
    context_neighbour_depth: Integer
    context_search_limit: Integer
    updated_by: core/Participant
    updated_at: Timestamp
}

entity LibrarianDialecticGate {
    librarian: harnesses/OwnerLibrarian
    conversation: conversations/Conversation
    opening_request: conversations/ConversationRequest
    practice: FormativePractice
    challenge: String
    status: DialecticGateStatus
    closing_request: conversations/ConversationRequest?
    opened_at: Timestamp
    closed_at: Timestamp?
}

entity LibrarianRuntimeRun {
    id: String
    librarian: harnesses/OwnerLibrarian
    manifest: manifests/AgentManifest?
    kind: LibrarianRunKind
    request_id: String?
    model_id: String
    status: LibrarianRunState
    started_at: Timestamp
    finished_at: Timestamp?
    output: String?
    error: String?
}

entity LibrarianContextReceipt {
    request: conversations/ConversationRequest
    participant: core/Participant
    within: List<core/Page>
    items: List<LibrarianContextItem>
    relations: List<LibrarianContextRelation>
    budget_characters: Integer
    used_characters: Integer
    omitted_page_blocks: Integer
    omitted_library_pages: Integer
    warnings: List<String>
    continuation: String?
}

entity LibrarianContextItem {
    receipt: LibrarianContextReceipt
    page: core/Page
    block: core/Block?
    revision: core/Revision
    authored_by: core/Participant
    found_by: List<ContextDiscovery>
    reason: String
    excerpt: String?
}

entity LibrarianContextRelation {
    receipt: LibrarianContextReceipt
    source: core/Page
    target: core/Page
    found_by: ContextDiscovery
    reason: String
}

actor LibrarianOwner {
    identified_by: core/Participant where this.kind = human and this.status = active
}

rule ComposeLibrarianContextReceipt {
    when: ComposeLibrarianContext(configuration, request, within, items, relations, used_characters, omitted_page_blocks, omitted_library_pages, warnings, continuation)
    requires: configuration.librarian.librarian = request.conversation.agent
    requires: within.all(page => readable(configuration.librarian.librarian, page))
    requires: items.all(item => within.contains(item.page))
    requires: relations.all(relation => within.contains(relation.source) and within.contains(relation.target))
    requires: items.all(item => item.revision = current_revision(item.block ?? item.page))
    requires: items.all(item => item.excerpt = null or revision_contains(item.revision, item.excerpt))
    requires: used_characters <= configuration.context_budget_characters or warnings.count > 0
    requires: omitted_page_blocks + omitted_library_pages = 0 or continuation != null
    ensures: LibrarianContextReceipt.created(
        request: request,
        participant: configuration.librarian.librarian,
        within: within,
        items: items,
        relations: relations,
        budget_characters: configuration.context_budget_characters,
        used_characters: used_characters,
        omitted_page_blocks: omitted_page_blocks,
        omitted_library_pages: omitted_library_pages,
        warnings: warnings,
        continuation: continuation
    )
}

rule OwnerConfiguresResidentRuntime {
    when: ConfigureLibrarianRuntime(owner, librarian, enabled, adapter, external_agent_id, model_id, endpoint, secret_reference, permissions, dialectic_enabled, routine_enabled, routine_hour, routine_timezone, context_budget_characters, context_neighbour_depth, context_search_limit)
    requires: librarian.owner = owner
    requires: not enabled or model_id != null
    requires: not enabled or adapter != external_agent or external_agent_id != null
    requires: routine_hour >= 0 and routine_hour <= 23
    requires: context_budget_characters >= 8000 and context_budget_characters <= 60000
    requires: context_neighbour_depth >= 0 and context_neighbour_depth <= 2
    requires: context_search_limit >= 0 and context_search_limit <= 20
    requires: not enabled or (permissions.contains(read_request_context) and permissions.contains(reply))
    requires: not routine_enabled or permissions.contains(daily_round)
    ensures: LibrarianRuntimeConfiguration.created(
        librarian: librarian,
        enabled: enabled,
        adapter: adapter,
        external_agent_id: external_agent_id,
        model_id: model_id,
        endpoint: endpoint,
        secret_reference: secret_reference,
        permissions: permissions,
        dialectic_enabled: dialectic_enabled,
        routine_enabled: routine_enabled,
        routine_hour: routine_hour,
        routine_timezone: routine_timezone,
        context_budget_characters: context_budget_characters,
        context_neighbour_depth: context_neighbour_depth,
        context_search_limit: context_search_limit,
        updated_by: owner,
        updated_at: now
    )
}

rule LibrarianOpensAFormativeThreshold {
    when: OpenDialecticGate(librarian, configuration, request, practice, challenge)
    requires: configuration.librarian = librarian
    requires: configuration.enabled
    requires: configuration.dialectic_enabled
    requires: request.conversation.agent = librarian.librarian
    requires: request.status = working
    requires: delegates_formative_practice(request, practice)
    requires: challenge != ""
    requires: not exists LibrarianDialecticGate{conversation: request.conversation, status: open}
    requires: not exists LibrarianDialecticGate{conversation: request.conversation, status: responding}
    ensures:
        request.status = answered
        request.finished_at = now
        conversations/AgentReply.created(
            request: request,
            answered_by: librarian.librarian,
            text: challenge,
            written_block: null,
            created_at: now
        )
        LibrarianDialecticGate.created(
            librarian: librarian,
            conversation: request.conversation,
            opening_request: request,
            practice: practice,
            challenge: challenge,
            status: open,
            closing_request: null,
            opened_at: now,
            closed_at: null
        )
}

rule HumanContributesAcrossTheThreshold {
    when: ContributeAcrossDialecticGate(human, gate, request)
    requires: gate.conversation.human = human
    requires: gate.status = open
    requires: request.conversation = gate.conversation
    requires: request.asked_by = human
    requires: request.text != ""
    ensures:
        gate.status = responding
        gate.closing_request = request
}

rule HumanExplicitlyBypassesTheThreshold {
    when: BypassDialecticGate(human, gate, request)
    requires: gate.conversation.human = human
    requires: gate.status = open
    requires: request.conversation = gate.conversation
    requires: request.asked_by = human
    ensures:
        gate.status = responding
        gate.closing_request = request
}

rule LibrarianCompletesTheDialectic {
    when: CompleteDialecticGate(librarian, gate, final_reply, bypassed)
    requires: gate.librarian = librarian
    requires: gate.status = responding
    requires: gate.closing_request != null
    requires: final_reply.request = gate.closing_request
    requires: final_reply.answered_by = librarian.librarian
    ensures:
        if bypassed:
            gate.status = bypassed
        else:
            gate.status = fulfilled
        gate.closed_at = now
}

rule FailedDialecticCompletionReopensTheThreshold {
    when: ReopenDialecticGateAfterFailure(librarian, gate)
    requires: gate.librarian = librarian
    requires: gate.status = responding
    ensures:
        gate.status = open
        gate.closing_request = null
}

rule EmbeddedRuntimeAnswersOneClaimedRequest {
    when: RunLibrarianRequest(configuration, request_id)
    requires: configuration.enabled
    requires: configuration.model_id != null
    requires: configuration.permissions.contains(read_request_context)
    requires: configuration.permissions.contains(reply)
    ensures: LibrarianRuntimeRun.created(
        id: generated_id,
        librarian: configuration.librarian,
        manifest: active_manifest(configuration.librarian.librarian),
        kind: request,
        request_id: request_id,
        model_id: configuration.model_id,
        status: completed,
        started_at: now,
        finished_at: now,
        output: generated_reply,
        error: null
    )
}

rule ResidentLibrarianInscribesStructuredWork {
    when: InscribeLibrarianWork(configuration, request, summary, blocks, changes, removals, lineage)
    requires: configuration.enabled
    requires: configuration.permissions.contains(reply)
    requires: request.conversation.agent = configuration.librarian.librarian
    requires: request.status = working
    requires: summary != ""
    requires: blocks.count > 0 or changes.count > 0
    requires: lineage.relation = direct or lineage.related_participant = request.asked_by
    requires: lineage.source_reference != null
    requires: blocks.all(block => block.content != "")
    requires: blocks.all(block => block.parent_key = null or blocks.any(parent => parent.key = block.parent_key))
    requires: blocks.all(block => not flattened_outline(block.content))
    requires: changes.all(change => not destructive(change) or removals.any(one => one.subject = subject_of(change)))
    requires: removals.all(one => summary.contains(one.chat_declaration))
    ensures:
        let reply = conversations/AgentReply.created(
            request: request,
            answered_by: configuration.librarian.librarian,
            text: summary,
            lineage: lineage,
            written_block: null,
            created_at: now
        )
        let inscription = LibrarianCorpusInscription.created(
            request: request,
            reply: reply,
            librarian: configuration.librarian.librarian,
            blocks: blocks,
            changes: changes,
            removals: removals,
            created_at: now
        )
        request.status = answered
        request.finished_at = now

    @guidance
        -- A correction request may split one old block into a tree, move its
        -- descendants or curate other pages. The visible conversation remains a
        -- compact receipt; the graph, operations and journal carry the work.
        -- Blocks materialize atomically as agent_generation using parent_key and
        -- position. Changes use fresh revisions and lineage. Every removal also
        -- creates its declaration under today's reserved librarian root before
        -- the request can become answered.
}

rule OwnerRunsTheDailyRound {
    when: RunLibrarianRoutine(owner, configuration)
    requires: configuration.librarian.owner = owner
    requires: configuration.enabled
    requires: configuration.permissions.contains(daily_round)
    ensures: LibrarianRuntimeRun.created(
        id: generated_id,
        librarian: configuration.librarian,
        manifest: active_manifest(configuration.librarian.librarian),
        kind: routine,
        request_id: null,
        model_id: configuration.model_id,
        status: completed,
        started_at: now,
        finished_at: now,
        output: generated_round,
        error: null
    )
}

invariant SecretsAreReferencesNotValues {
    for configuration in LibrarianRuntimeConfigurations:
        configuration.secret_reference = null or
        not configuration.secret_reference.contains("Bearer ")
}

invariant OneRuntimeConfigurationPerOwnerLibrarian {
    for a in LibrarianRuntimeConfigurations:
        for b in LibrarianRuntimeConfigurations:
            a.librarian = b.librarian implies a = b
}

surface LibrarianRuntimeAdministration {
    facing owner: LibrarianOwner
    context configuration: LibrarianRuntimeConfiguration where configuration.librarian.owner = owner

    exposes:
        configuration.librarian
        configuration.enabled
        configuration.model_id
        configuration.endpoint
        configuration.secret_reference
        configuration.permissions
        configuration.dialectic_enabled
        configuration.routine_enabled
        configuration.routine_hour
        configuration.routine_timezone
        configuration.context_budget_characters
        configuration.context_neighbour_depth
        configuration.context_search_limit
        for run in LibrarianRuntimeRuns where librarian = configuration.librarian:
            run.kind
            run.model_id
            run.status
            run.started_at
            run.finished_at
            run.output
            run.error

    provides:
        ConfigureLibrarianRuntime(owner, configuration.librarian, enabled, adapter, external_agent_id, model_id, endpoint, secret_reference, permissions, dialectic_enabled, routine_enabled, routine_hour, routine_timezone, context_budget_characters, context_neighbour_depth, context_search_limit)
        RunLibrarianRoutine(owner, configuration)

    contracts:
        fulfils ResidentLibrarianExecution

    @guarantee RuntimeIdentityIsTheConstitutedLibrarian
        -- La bibliotecaria responde con su participante. Cotito puede seguir
        -- operando por el puente externo, pero nunca firma como Lucienne.

    @guarantee OneClaimHasOneWinner
        -- El runtime embebido y un puente externo pueden coexistir. La primera
        -- reclamación atómica gana y la otra recibe que el turno ya no está en cola.

    @guarantee ActivationRequiresAnExplicitHumanAct
        -- Constituir una bibliotecaria o migrar una instalación no inicia un
        -- modelo ni una rutina. La persona elige modelo, permisos y activación.

    @guarantee RoutinesBeginDisabled
        -- Una ronda automática nace apagada y también puede ejecutarse a mano.

    @guarantee LargePagesAndManifestsDoNotOverflowTheModelContext
        -- La solicitud y el manifiesto permanecen íntegros como recibos durables,
        -- pero el prompt recibe proyecciones acotadas que priorizan identidad,
        -- gobierno, foco, estructura y pasajes pertinentes. Una página o
        -- constitución grande no hace fallar una pregunta breve.

    @guarantee ModelFailuresDoNotPersistThePrompt
        -- Un fallo local registra un diagnóstico acotado. La línea de comandos,
        -- que contiene el prompt y su contexto privado, nunca queda en el recibo.

    @guarantee RoutinesOnlyReportOperationalEvidence
        -- Una ronda no encarga al modelo inventar diagnósticos a partir de
        -- conteos. Sin violaciones observadas responde SIN_NOVEDAD; con ellas
        -- enumera únicamente los controles que Vera comprobó y sus detalles.

    @guarantee EveryRunLeavesPublicOperationalEvidence
        -- Vera conserva modelo, manifiesto, comienzo, término, estado, salida o
        -- error. No conserva razonamiento privado ni el valor del secreto.

    @guarantee ExternalClaimsLeaveTheSameRuntimeEvidence
        -- Claiming an external request starts a run and replying or failing it
        -- closes that run. Administration exposes queue, work and total elapsed
        -- time from the durable request and run timestamps; an external adapter
        -- is not an observability exception.

    @guarantee ProvenanceIsDeclaredBeforeInscription
        -- The responder explicitly chooses direct, mediated, derived or
        -- coauthored for every substantive inscription. Vera preserves the
        -- request page, block, recording or conversation as source and refuses
        -- a non-direct relation that omits the requesting participant.

    @guarantee BroadLibraryQuestionsBeginWithARecordedSurvey
        -- Una petición sobre conjuntos de páginas, proyectos, tareas o relaciones
        -- comienza por una inspección gobernada del corpus. El modelo puede pedir
        -- lecturas posteriores, pero no decidir que buscar era innecesario.

    @guarantee TheOriginalTaskSurvivesEveryFollowUp
        -- Aclaraciones, aportes mayéuticos, preguntas sobre progreso y bypasses
        -- conservan el encargo abierto. La respuesta final resuelve ese encargo,
        -- no sólo la frase más reciente.
}

actor LibrarianConversationHuman {
    identified_by: core/Participant where this.kind = human and this.status = active
}

surface LibrarianDialecticConversation {
    facing human: LibrarianConversationHuman
    context gate: LibrarianDialecticGate where conversation.human = human

    exposes:
        gate.practice
        gate.challenge
        gate.status
        gate.opening_request
        gate.closing_request

    provides:
        ContributeAcrossDialecticGate(human, gate, request) when gate.status = open
        BypassDialecticGate(human, gate, request) when gate.status = open

    @guarantee FinalAnswerWaitsForAContributionOrExplicitBypass
        -- El desafío puede orientar o reducir la consigna, pero no contiene
        -- subrepticiamente el trabajo final. El harness sólo permite completarlo
        -- después de una tentativa humana o de un bypass visible y deliberado.

    @guarantee OperationalRequestsRemainDirect
        -- Buscar, citar, verificar, recuperar, ordenar, transcribir, enlazar,
        -- completar metadatos, clasificar, etiquetar, reordenar, explicar el
        -- corpus, formatear o ejecutar una decisión ya tomada no abre un umbral.
        -- Una fuente identificable tampoco debe quedar detrás de una pregunta
        -- formativa.

    @guarantee AClueCountsAsContribution
        -- Una pista, hipótesis, fuente o criterio ya aportado basta para ayudar
        -- directamente. La persona no tiene que repetir esa contribución en la
        -- forma que prefiera el agente.

    @guarantee DeterminedWorkComesBeforeAQuestion
        -- Si una solicitud mezcla recuperación factual y juicio, el agente
        -- completa primero la parte determinada. Puede formular como máximo una
        -- pregunta breve sobre la decisión personal restante, sin retener lo ya
        -- encontrado.

    @guarantee ResearchPrecedesAnyFormativeQuestion
        -- La palabra «síntesis» no convierte una investigación bibliotecaria en
        -- un examen. Cuando hay corpus que recuperar, clasificar o relacionar,
        -- toda esa labor se completa antes de ofrecer una pregunta de juicio.

    @guarantee MayeuticsIsAnOfferNotAnAccessCondition
        -- Una petición explícita de ejecución directa o la insistencia posterior
        -- cierran la resistencia sin contraseña social, reproche ni otro desafío.

    @guarantee OneOpenThresholdPerConversation
        -- Una conversación no acumula exámenes ni bucles de desafíos. El turno
        -- que responde a un umbral debe recibir una respuesta final.
}
